# Tilted drain: P1, launch, nudges until tilt (as d_nudge.uh: tilt at frame 481), then a drain.
# BallDrainControl with the tilt lock set: no bonus text, next ball: mode == 10 (tilt_lock == 0) at 731.
# bonus_step is 9, not 0, after a tilted drain: with the lock set Mode11BonusController starts at step 8
# (dragon_bonus.cpp:129-130) and the step loop makes it 9; Wine shows the same value (dragon_tilt_pause timeline
# bonus_step 0 -> 9 at t=19.762, mode 10, tilt_lock 0). Because 9 is also what an untilted drain with nothing earned
# ends at, a bonus is earned first (a_spot4 at 150 is the skill shot: mode 2, one spell, targets_hit 1 at 487), so the
# tilt skip is what keeps bonus text ids 3012 (targets) and 3015 (spells) off the display from the drain on.
# The 2.5 s tilt_lock interval of Wine is not checked natively here (tilt_lock is already 0 at 505: the drain is forced at 500).
init window 960 666
init fixed_dt 10
init seed 1
init dump_period 10
10 key down new_game
11 key up new_game
150 event a_spot4 ControlCollision
151 expect mode == 2
200 key down plunger
300 key up plunger
400 key down bump_left
410 key up bump_left
425 key down bump_right
435 key up bump_right
450 key down bump_left
460 key up bump_left
475 key down bump_right
485 key up bump_right
486 expect tilt_lock == 1
487 expect targets_hit == 1
500 place 0 0 15.6 0.37 0 1 5 0x1
510 expect bonus_step == 9
730 expect bonus_step == 9
731 expect mode == 10
505-730 expect none text info_text_box display id 3012
505-730 expect none text info_text_box display id 3015
731 expect tilt_lock == 0
900 quit
